msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:5
msgid "Philosophy"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"FitTrackee was created specifically to completely avoid proprietary web "
"platforms for tracking sports activities.<br />Workout files contain "
"sensitive data related to location and health."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:10
msgid ""
"This is one of the reasons why, for example, automatic synchronization of"
" an account hosted on proprietary web platform is not integrated into "
"FitTrackee.<br />For the time being, files must therefore be added "
"manually or third-party tools must be used (or developed) for this type "
"of synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:13
msgid ""
"The other important point is that FitTrackee must be easy to install, "
"particularly for use by a single user and without interaction, for which "
"Python and a PostgreSQL/PostGIS database are sufficient.<br />Ideally, it"
" should be possible to install it on low-resource servers such as the "
"Raspberry Pi 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:16
msgid ""
"Pull requests or feature requests must therefore take these points into "
"account."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:18
msgid "Report issues, ask for features"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:20
msgid "If a bug is a security vulnerability, please refer to security policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:22
msgid ""
"Ensure an issue was not already opened by searching on Codeberg under "
"Issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/contributing.md:24
